# Copy Rules

- Write as a craftsperson would speak: concrete details (materials, dimensions, lead time) over abstract adjectives.
- Forbidden words: "elevate", "seamless", "unleash", "transform your space", "game-changer", "delve", "tapestry", "robust", "foster".
- Avoid the "rule of three" (three parallel adjectives/clauses). One precise detail beats three vague ones.
- No rhetorical questions in headings.
- CTA text = verb + object: "Написать в WhatsApp", "Заказать замер". Never "Узнать больше" / "Подробнее".
- For Russian copy: use em-dashes sparingly, as a human editor would.